Review the diff below (plangraph RT-P1-GOVERNOR, HIGH: keeper schema + migration + auth-adjacent verbs). Answer each vector V1..V5 under its own heading with file:function evidence; say PASS or a concrete defect (input -> wrong output).
V1 keeper/schema.py:METRICS_DDL, keeper/db.py:_upgrade, keeper/schema_pg.py:_V4 + MIGRATIONS: SQLite/Postgres column parity, idempotent upgrade of a v10 database, no DDL that the keeper connection's authorizer would deny at upgrade, copy_to_pg table order.
V2 keeper/store_metrics.py:_set_metrics / _get_metrics: role gating (router/system only to write), validation completeness (day, metric name, value finiteness/bool, source), atomicity of a mixed batch, SQL injection / portability (? placeholders, ON CONFLICT), row cap.
